GAL22V10
VJIOR5

IORQn A2 A3 A4 A5 A6 A7 RESETn M1n WRn PICINT GND
GND0 PICCSn PPICSn UARTCSn PITCSn POSTCLK IORESET INTn INTAn NC NC VCC

; Four-port granularity uses A2-A7. M1 must be high for every peripheral
; select, excluding the Z80 interrupt-acknowledge cycle.
/PICCSn  = /IORQn * M1n * /A7 * /A6 * /A5 * /A4 * /A3 * /A2
/PPICSn  = /IORQn * M1n * /A7 * /A6 * /A5 * /A4 * /A3 *  A2
/UARTCSn = /IORQn * M1n * /A7 * /A6 * /A5 * /A4 *  A3 * /A2
/PITCSn  = /IORQn * M1n * /A7 * /A6 * /A5 *  A4 *  A3 * /A2

; ACT273 clocks at the end of a write to 20h-23h: low during the selected
; active-low write pulse, positive edge when WR_N/IORQ_N is released.
POSTCLK = IORQn + /M1n + WRn + A7 + A6 + /A5 + A4 + A3 + A2

IORESET = /RESETn

; The shared bus interrupt is open-drain: drive only zero while PIC_INT is high.
INTn.T = GND
INTn.E = PICINT

/INTAn = /M1n * /IORQn

DESCRIPTION

VJUGA rev B I/O U2: M1-qualified PIC/PPI/USART/D57, POST clock, reset and IRQ.
